20:Sakura...
21:Besides...
22:I've never seen you lose so badly before.
23:Hehe, maybe today the goddess of luck will smile on me and I'll come out on top.
25:Okay, I look forward to playing against you when the time comes.

29:As expected, Archer, you're as efficient as ever.
31:Fu Ji, did you confirm the target's appearance?
32:Yep.
42:S-Sure.
44:Shirou... It won't be long now.
46:It's headline news – looks like I got involved in something big, nyaa!
48:Yes, it was indeed very dangerous.
50:...Huh? Oh, yep. That's right.
56:After going through all this trouble, the rumor turned out to be false.
58:...I guess you're right.
62:What is it, nyaa?
63:Can Tohsaka senpai and I also participate in the competition held at your place during the weekend?
64:Now that I'm finally enjoying mahjong, I want to play it more.
65:Oh, that would be great, nyaa!
68:No problem. Thank you so much!
70:What is it, Sakura?
73:Yeah, yeah. Let's just get him first.
74:Shirou... I'm so glad.
78:Take care, nyaa!
79:...
80:Yes, goodbye!
89:Where the Journey Goes
95:Outside the Competition Venue
96:Kidnappers' Hideout
97:One Han City - Some Restaurant
100:The only thing I remember about yesterday is that we had a blast playing mahjong, nyaa! Oh, and I slept so well after all that winning, nyaa!
105:Um... I don't know either. I'll have to do well in the competition to lure out the kidnappers, but I'm not sure how far I can get.
106:But maybe yesterday's class changed something in me. I feel like I've started to enjoy mahjong a bit more, and I'm even a little excited about the competition.
108:It's true. I was all over the place yesterday, but it was my first time playing mahjong with Tohsaka senpai, after all...
111:Spotting someone acting suspiciously during the competition, tracking them to their hideout, confirming that the suspects are gathering inside, and then staying under the radar to keep watch...
112:Something this trivial isn't worth praising. They were just a group of ordinary people.
113:The people who kidnapped me were among them. They are definitely the kidnappers.
114:Shirou and the other hostages are most likely in there too. We just need to take down all the kidnappers and rescue the victims. I don't think we need a very detailed plan now.
116:I've been meaning to ask you this for a while. Are you sure you two can handle that?
117:If the plan is just to subdue the kidnappers, it's safer for us to take care of it. That way, there's no risk of the victims getting hurt.
118:Just a reminder – don't go overboard. This is the city, and there are no Overseers here.
119:You don't need to remind me of that. Still, I'm not planning to go easy on them – not after they kidnapped so many innocent people for their own selfish desires.
121:If you need a hand, you can ask that nosy red-haired kid among the victims for help.
122:Let's do it then, Saber. It's a shame our opponents are so weak. They aren't worthy of us teaming up.
123:So in the end, all the kidnappers got arrested, all the hostages were rescued safe and sound, and... half of the hideout building was blown up, nyaa!
127:...Yeah. The world's so huge, and there's so much we don't know. I never thought something like that, um...
128:Huh...? I guess so. I've never seen a gas explosion take place in front of me either.
129:Anyway, it's good that everything worked out in the end. Let's just forget about the gas explosion – no point in dwelling on something that's already happened.
130:Yes, I'm glad that senpai is safe and sound.
131:Chin up. We came here just to check it out. It's not like we were really expecting anything anyway.
133:The results, huh? How should I put it? It wasn't really a win or a loss. I guess we'll have to determine the winner next time.
138:It was the police. They told me that the investigation senpai stayed over to assist with is almost wrapped up, and he can come back soon.
139:We need to hurry and pick him up...! What should I bring for him? A change of clothes, his wallet... What else am I forgetting...
140:Let's go, Sakura. Who knows what else Emiya can get caught up in if we leave him alone?
142:...You're welcome. Take care!
143:I'll leave the competition to you, Ichihime, Rin, and Sakura.
144:Huh? Fu Ji, aren't you coming with us, nyaa?
145:Didn't I tell you yesterday? I saw the kidnappers' faces, so it's better for me to track them... Have you forgotten already?
146:I don't think anything unexpected will go down at the competition, but you should still be careful just in case.
147:Thank you, Saber. I hope everything goes well on your side too.
148:Rin, you better not get too thrilled about the competition and let your guard down.
149:Seriously, what sort of person do you think I am? Stop talking now and go find the kidnappers!
150:...This guy, I swear. Anyway, how are you, Sakura? Feeling confident?
151:You are a strange one. I don't get how you could start liking mahjong after what happened yesterday. Ichihime was basically the only one winning.
152:...Hmph, we'll see about that. If we both keep advancing, don't expect me to go easy on you when we face off.
153:Hey, you two! The competition is about to start, nyaa! Come quickly, nyaa!
154:Yes, that's right. There's no way we can mess up something as simple as this.
155:...Fu Ji, after we rescue the victims, please guide them out of the building as soon as possible.
156:Speaking of which, I still can't believe there was a gas explosion at the building you tracked the kidnappers to. It was such a close call, nyaa. Thank goodness you guys and the hostages got out early; otherwise, you could have been seriously injured, nyaa...
157:The victims all made it out safely thanks to Fu Ji's quick actions. Thank you very much.
158:Is something wrong, Fu Ji? You've seemed a bit out of it since yesterday, nyaa! Did the gas explosion really throw you off that much, nyaa?
159:By the way, Rin and Sakura, how did yesterday's mahjong competition go? I still haven't asked you about the results.
160:Oh, Miss Ichihime, can I discuss something with you?
161:Okay! We better practice hard since we're going to compete on the weekend! Fu Ji, you have to help us too!
162:Sure. As long as you pay enough Coppers, I'm more than willing to help. I promise fair treatment for all, no tricks.
163:Hello? Yes, hi... Yes, okay. I understand. Thank you very much.
164:O-Okay...! Miss Ichihime, Miss Fu Ji, thank you for helping us this time and for agreeing to my earlier request!
